the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/fd/fd221ae68fc4983fb0a3f7a745154764e5c0081b2b9b66e7f8ad4a150a8b3bc5.png)\n\nNotice that the positive orientations of the inner curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are opposite to those stated in the question.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =(- \\frac{25}{3})-\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{13}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-50)-32-39}{6} \\\\  & =- \\frac{121}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543834 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04fa1ed4-4d14-540d-97de-17e4ea742baa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543807} {:answer/id #uuid "0ed577c8-30fd-548a-b930-79b44fab958d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{91}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543810} {:answer/id #uuid "58497438-3492-546e-943f-9a79c035517d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{29}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543816} {:answer/id #uuid "b5b06cad-9359-531f-99db-dcc71b377046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543829} {:answer/id #uuid "bd10c665-5dc5-55ab-9e3d-c447f60443ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{29}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 175921865438